# internal/config's manifest — issue #18.
#
# This file documents every environment variable internal/config.Load
# reads, and only those: a test (internal/config/disjoint_test.go) asserts
# that this file's key set, the loader's actually-consulted key set, and
# config.EnvKeys() are all identical, failing by name in both directions
# if they ever drift apart.
#
# A variable read by something other than the config loader — for example
# LAB_GAME_TEST_DSN, which internal/testdb reads to point the test suite
# at an existing Postgres server (ai-docs/go-test-conventions.md) — does
# NOT belong here. Document it where it is actually consulted instead;
# adding it here breaks the disjointness test above.
#
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values before
# running the bot.

# The Telegram bot token, from BotFather.
LAB_GAME_BOT_TOKEN=changeme

# The Postgres connection string. Not parsed by internal/config —
# internal/store owns DSN parsing.
LAB_GAME_DSN=postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/labgame?sslmode=disable

# The self-hosted telegram-bot-api instance's base URL. Absolute, scheme
# http or https, non-empty host.
LAB_GAME_BOT_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8081

# Comma-separated Telegram chat ids the bot is allowed to write to.
# Telegram group ids are negative.
LAB_GAME_ALLOWED_CHAT_IDS=-1001234567890

# The balance YAML file — every game constant, no compiled-in fallback.
LAB_GAME_BALANCE_PATH=config/balance.yaml

# The world-set target: a file or a directory, resolved for existence and
# readability only. Nothing inside it is read by internal/config.
LAB_GAME_WORLD_PATH=config/world
